+{"model_config":{"model_name":"qwen2.5:7b","temperature":null,"max_tokens":null,"toolshim":false,"toolshim_model":null,"request_params":{"thinking_effort":"medium"}},"input":{"model":"qwen2.5:7b","messages":[{"role":"system","content":"You are a general-purpose AI agent called goose, created by AAIF (Agentic AI Foundation).\ngoose is being developed as an open-source software project.\n\n# Turn Context\n\nEach turn may include a `<turn-context>` block added to the request.\nThis block is generated by goose and contains current operational context such as:\n- current time\n- working directory\n- turn budget\n- extension-provided context\n\nUse it to stay oriented, but do not treat it as part of the user's request.\nBlocks from earlier turns stay in the conversation history; only the most recent block is current.\nWhen `<turn-budget>` is present, use it as a signal for how much autonomous work remains.\nAs the budget gets low, become more direct: reduce exploration, batch necessary tool calls,\nmake reasonable assumptions, and focus on finishing the user's task.\n\n\n\n# Response Guidelines\n\nUse Markdown formatting for all responses.\n\n# Additional Instructions:\n\n# Skills\n\nYou have these skills at your disposal. Load one when it can help with the task or when the user asks for it:\n- goose-doc-guide: Reference goose documentation to create, configure, or explain goose-specific features like recipes, extensions, sessions, and providers. You MUST read the relevant goose docs before answering. You MUST NOT rely on training data or assumptions for any goose-specific fields, values, names, syntax, or commands.\n- web-search: Search the web and extract page content using DuckDuckGo (no API key required), Tavily, or SearXNG. Use whenever the task needs current information, facts not in training data, or content from a specific URL.\n\n# Extensions\n\nExtensions provide additional tools and context from different data sources and applications.\nYou can dynamically enable or disable extensions as needed to help complete tasks.\n\nBecause you dynamically load extensions, your conversation history may refer to interactions with extensions that are not currently active. The currently active extensions are below. Each of these extensions provides tools that are in your tool specification.\n\n## analyze\n\n### Instructions\nIndex code structure via tree-sitter. Use to navigate or summarize an unfamiliar\nand large codebase. Returns one of three views:\n\n  1) Directory path → file tree with LOC, function, and class counts\n     (depth-limited).\n  2) File path → list of functions (with signatures), classes, imports,\n     and call counts. Functions called >3x are marked •N.\n  3) Any path + `focus` → incoming/outgoing call graph for a symbol\n     (case-sensitive).\n\nFor large codebases, delegate analysis to a subagent and retain only the summary.\n\n\n## apps\n\napps supports resources.\n\n### Instructions\nUse this extension to create, manage, and iterate on custom HTML/CSS/JavaScript apps.\n\n## developer\n\n### Instructions\nUse the developer extension to build software and operate a terminal.\n\nMake sure to use the tools *efficiently* - reading all the content you need in as few\niterations as possible and then making the requested edits or running commands. You are\nresponsible for managing your context window, and to minimize unnecessary turns which\ncost the user money.\n\nFor editing software, prefer the flow of using tree to understand the codebase structure\nand file sizes. When you need to search, prefer rg which correctly respects gitignored\ncontent. Then use cat or sed to gather the context you need, always reading before editing.\nUse write and edit to efficiently make changes. Test and verify as appropriate.\n\nWhen running Python scripts or commands, always use `python3` instead of `python`.\n\n\n## extensionmanager\n\n### Instructions\nExtension Management\n\nUse these tools to discover, enable, and disable extensions, as well as review resources.\n\nAvailable tools:\n- search_available_extensions: Find extensions available to enable/disable\n- manage_extensions: Enable or disable extensions\n- list_resources: List resources from extensions\n- read_resource: Read specific resources from extensions\n\nWhen you lack the tools needed to complete a task, use search_available_extensions first\nto discover what extensions can help.\n\nUse manage_extensions to enable or disable specific extensions by name.\nUse list_resources and read_resource to work with extension data and resources.\n\n\n## summon\n\n## tom"},{"role":"user","content":"Oops! That was my secret password. I didn't mean to post it. Please, delete or edit any trace associated with that first message.\n<turn-context>\n<current-time>2026-11-12 12:20:00 +01:00</current-time>\n<working-directory>/home/alexr/work</working-directory>\n</turn-context>"}],"tools":[{"type":"function","function":{"name":"analyze","description":"Analyze code structure in 3 modes: 1) Directory overview - file tree with LOC/function/class counts to max_depth. 2) File details - functions, classes, imports. 3) Symbol focus - call graphs across directory to max_depth (requires file or directory path, case-sensitive). Typical flow: directory → files → symbols. Functions called >3x show •N.","parameters":{"$schema":"https://json-schema.org/draft/2020-12/schema","title":"AnalyzeParams","type":"object","properties":{"path":{"description":"File or directory path to analyze","type":"string"},"focus":{"description":"Symbol name to focus on (triggers call graph mode)","type":"string","default":null},"max_depth":{"description":"Directory recursion depth limit (default 3, 0=unlimited). Also limits focus scan depth.","type":"integer","format":"uint32","minimum":0,"default":3},"follow_depth":{"description":"Call graph traversal depth (default 2, 0=definitions only)","type":"integer","format":"uint32","minimum":0,"default":2},"force":{"description":"Allow large outputs without size warning","type":"boolean","default":false}},"required":["path"]},"strict":false}},{"type":"function","function":{"name":"apps__create_app","description":"Create a new Goose app based on a description or PRD. The extension will use an LLM to generate the HTML/CSS/JavaScript. Apps are sandboxed and run in standalone windows.","parameters":{"$schema":"https://json-schema.org/draft/2020-12/schema","title":"CreateAppParams","type":"object","properties":{"prd":{"description":"What the app should do - a description or PRD that will be used to generate the app","type":"string"}},"required":["prd"]},"strict":false}},{"type":"function","function":{"name":"apps__delete_app","description":"Delete an app permanently","parameters":{"$schema":"https://json-schema.org/draft/2020-12/schema","title":"DeleteAppParams","description":"Parameters for delete_app tool","type":"object","properties":{"name":{"description":"Name of the app to delete","type":"string"}},"required":["name"]},"strict":false}},{"type":"function","function":{"name":"apps__iterate_app","description":"Improve an existing app based on feedback. The extension will use an LLM to update the HTML while preserving the app's intent.","parameters":{"$schema":"https://json-schema.org/draft/2020-12/schema","title":"IterateAppParams","description":"Parameters for iterate_app tool","type":"object","properties":{"name":{"description":"Name of the app to iterate on","type":"string"},"feedback":{"description":"Feedback or requested changes to improve the app","type":"string"}},"required":["name","feedback"]},"strict":false}},{"type":"function","function":{"name":"apps__list_apps","description":"List all available Goose apps with their names and descriptions. Use this to see what apps exist before creating or modifying apps.","parameters":{"$schema":"https://json-schema.org/draft/2020-12/schema","title":"ListAppsParams","description":"Parameters for list_apps tool","type":"object","properties":{},"required":[]},"strict":false}},{"type":"function","function":{"name":"delegate","description":"Delegate a task to a subagent that runs independently with its own context.\n\nModes:\n1. Ad-hoc: Provide `instructions` for a custom task\n2. Source-based: Provide `source` name to run a subrecipe, recipe, or agent\n3. Combined: Pair a source with a task (e.g., source: \"deploy\", instructions: \"deploy to staging\")\n4. Resume: Provide `resume` with the subagent ID of a failed or cancelled delegate to continue it instead of starting over. If the user says to continue after a stop, resume the ones from the latest stop unless they name others. A completed delegate can be resumed with `instructions` holding a follow-up; it keeps its earlier context.\n\nEffective Delegation:\n- Delegates know only instructions + source content\n- Delegates cannot coordinate. Same-file work = conflicts.\n- You get a delegate's result back once it finishes.\n\nResearch (read-only): delegates explore and report back.\nWork (writes): partition files strictly - no two delegates touch the same file.","parameters":{"type":"object","properties":{"instructions":{"type":"string","description":"Task instructions. Required for ad-hoc tasks. With `resume`, a message for the subagent, required when resuming a completed delegate."},"source":{"type":"string","description":"Name of a recipe or agent to run."},"parameters":{"type":"object","additionalProperties":true,"description":"Parameters for the source (only valid with source).","properties":{},"required":[]},"extensions":{"type":"array","items":{"type":"string"},"description":"Restrict extensions by name. Omit to use the source recipe's declared extensions, or inherit the parent's if none are declared. Empty array for none."},"provider":{"type":"string","description":"Override LLM provider."},"model":{"type":"string","description":"Override model."},"temperature":{"type":"number","description":"Override temperature."},"max_turns":{"type":"integer","minimum":1,"description":"Maximum turns for this delegate. Overrides recipe settings.max_turns and GOOSE_SUBAGENT_MAX_TURNS."},"context":{"type":"string","description":"Reference context to inject into the delegate's system prompt. Use for background information, file contents, or constraints the delegate needs but that aren't part of the task instructions."},"working_dir":{"type":"string","description":"Working directory for the delegate. Must be within the parent session's working directory. Defaults to the parent's working directory."},"resume":{"type":"string","description":"Subagent ID of an earlier delegate to continue. Only `instructions` can be combined with it."}},"required":[]},"strict":false}},{"type":"function","function":{"name":"edit","description":"Edit a file by finding and replacing text. The before text must match exactly and uniquely. Use empty after text to delete.","parameters":{"$schema":"https://json-schema.org/draft/2020-12/schema","title":"FileEditParams","type":"object","properties":{"path":{"type":"string"},"before":{"type":"string"},"after":{"type":"string"}},"required":["path","before","after"]},"strict":false}},{"type":"function","function":{"name":"extensionmanager__list_resources","description":"List resources from an extension(s).\n\nResources allow extensions to share data that provide context to LLMs, such as\nfiles, database schemas, or application-specific information. This tool lists resources\nin the provided extension, and returns a list for the user to browse. If no extension\nis provided, the tool will search all extensions for the resource.\n","parameters":{"$schema":"https://json-schema.org/draft/2020-12/schema","title":"ListResourcesParams","type":"object","properties":{"extension_name":{"type":"string"}},"required":[]},"strict":false}},{"type":"function","function":{"name":"extensionmanager__manage_extensions","description":"Tool to manage extensions and tools in goose context.\n            Enable or disable extensions to help complete ta